1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,218
What if the world forgot one word every day?

2
00:00:03,258 --> 00:00:05,269
Monday, nobody can say cheese.

3
00:00:05,309 --> 00:00:07,525
The sign above the shop flickers,

4
00:00:07,565 --> 00:00:11,559
the letters melt, and everyone just points at the sandwich.

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,914
Tuesday, it's the word umbrella.

6
00:00:13,954 --> 00:00:14,985
Wednesday, bicycle.

7
00:00:15,025 --> 00:00:16,732
You invent clumsy replacements,

8
00:00:16,772 --> 00:00:18,649
like rain hat and two-wheel horse.

9
00:00:18,689 --> 00:00:21,073
Dictionaries shrink a little every morning,

10
00:00:21,113 --> 00:00:22,877
like autumn trees losing leaves.

11
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:26,089
By week two, people start talking in gestures.

12
00:00:26,129 --> 00:00:28,747
Waiters mime orders, teachers draw pictures,

13
00:00:28,787 --> 00:00:31,284
and street signs become tiny comic strips.

14
00:00:31,324 --> 00:00:34,063
Honestly, it's quieter, and kind of beautiful.

15
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:35,734
By day one hundred,

16
00:00:35,774 --> 00:00:37,926
the big words start vanishing too.

17
00:00:37,966 --> 00:00:38,506
Tomorrow.

18
00:00:38,546 --> 00:00:38,892
Sorry.

19
00:00:38,932 --> 00:00:39,343
Friend.

20
00:00:39,383 --> 00:00:40,632
Nobody can say them,

21
00:00:40,672 --> 00:00:41,986
so people hold doors,

22
00:00:42,026 --> 00:00:44,564
share umbrellas, and bring soup instead.

23
00:00:44,604 --> 00:00:46,368
Actions speak louder anyway.

24
00:00:46,850 --> 00:00:49,058
Scientists would call this impossible,

25
00:00:49,098 --> 00:00:51,129
since words don't vanish overnight.

26
00:00:51,169 --> 00:00:52,726
In this thought experiment,

27
00:00:52,766 --> 00:00:55,507
though, language slowly empties like a bathtub,

28
00:00:55,547 --> 00:00:57,578
and you can almost hear the gurgle.

29
00:00:58,050 --> 00:00:59,056
Day two hundred.

30
00:00:59,096 --> 00:01:00,689
The word love disappears.

31
00:01:00,729 --> 00:01:03,695
Couples stare at each other, completely stuck.

32
00:01:03,735 --> 00:01:05,068
Then, without a word,

33
00:01:05,108 --> 00:01:06,505
he hands her an apple,

34
00:01:06,545 --> 00:01:08,335
and she hands him her scarf.

35
00:01:09,550 --> 00:01:10,683
Here's the twist.

36
00:01:10,723 --> 00:01:13,166
When the dictionary is nearly empty,

37
00:01:13,206 --> 00:01:15,442
people invent new words together.

38
00:01:15,482 --> 00:01:17,028
Gloop means happy rain.

39
00:01:17,068 --> 00:01:19,167
Fizz means a hug from far away.

40
00:01:19,207 --> 00:01:21,374
Language is never gone for long.

41
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:24,707
So every morning, the town gathers to invent

42
00:01:24,747 --> 00:01:26,353
tomorrow's word together.

43
00:01:26,393 --> 00:01:28,263
Today's winner is a tiny kid,

44
00:01:28,303 --> 00:01:30,897
who points at the sunrise and says: wow.

45
00:01:30,937 --> 00:01:31,950
Everyone agrees.

46
00:01:31,990 --> 00:01:33,267
It means everything.
